/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Source-free means the independent source is removed or switched out at t = 0.
   - L is inductance in henry (H); R is resistance in ohm (Ω); i is the loop current in ampere (A) at time t in second (s).
   - The solution is i(t) = I₀ e−t/τ with τ = L/R.
   - τ is the time constant, measured in seconds.
   - Differentiate x(t) = x(0)e−t/τ at t = 0: slope = −x(0)/τ.
   - R changes the two circuits in opposite ways.
   - Stored energy is ½ L I₀² in the inductor and ½ C V₀² in the capacitor.
*/
