/* book exam traps: Writing τ = R/L for an RL circuit or τ = 1/(RC) for an RC circuit. Check units: τ must come out in seconds. | Writing 63.2 % at t = τ for a decay. A source-free decay has 36.8 % of its starting value left at t = τ; 63.2 % of the final value belongs to a charging curve. | Treating 5τ as exactly zero. About 0.67 % is left, so an exam may ask for the exact expression. | Forgetting that I₀ or V₀ comes from the instant before switching. The inductor current and capacitor voltage cannot jump; see initial and final conditions. | Saying a large R always slows decay. In RL, τ = L/R falls as R rises; in RC, τ = RC rises as R rises. */
